														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3728698">
									

<p>I think this is the most I've been torn on an SCP, <em>ever.</em></p>
<p>I really, really wanted to like this. The idea of a man always being forced to be the last person alive in the universe is both ambitious and great fodder for pathos. Your efforts to describe in-detail the Foundation's relationship with other universes is very interesting, if a bit contrived.</p>
<p>However, I find myself compelled to -1 for the lack of the aforementioned pathos. Your article is about one of the most horrifying things that can happen to a person and yet, fundamentally, lacks humanity. How does Lloyd feel about this? What is it like to experience this over and over again? These were questions I hoped would be addressed, but never were.</p>
<p>This is a technically solid and intellectually fascinating work, but I require humanoid SCPs to emotionally engage me, and this just didn't at all.</p>

							</div>

								
					
