			<div class="content" id="post-content-3729346">
									

<p>This is pretty cool, but I'm a little confused in a few places:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Should the probability of SCP-3856-1's imminent death rise above 0.01% at any time, <strong>they</strong> are to be immediately ejected to the nearest inhabited universe.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The full range of SCP-3856's effects are not known, but the primary element appears to be the fact that Researcher Lloyd will inevitably (100% chance, no observed margin of error) cease brain activity only following the elimination of every other extant human (defined as a non-anomalous instance of homo sapiens, native to the relevant universe) within the universe in which <strong>they</strong> currently reside.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Addendum.1: Event 3856-Alpha: On ██/██/████, despite agreed-upon travel protocols, a single instance of Researcher Lloyd manifested within Site-54, equipped with standard Foundation provisions and equipment (circa 1880 AD). They were later determined to have originated from U-4046Y</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What are &quot;they&quot;? Does &quot;they&quot; refer to multiple instances of Researcher Lloyd?</p>

